# The build context for session.Dockerfile, and nothing else.
#
# BuildKit reads "<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore" in preference to a root .dockerignore,
# so this scopes the filter to this one image instead of claiming a repository-root file
# every future image build would share.
#
# An allowlist, and that is the whole design. The repository root is 5.5 GB -- .claude is
# 4.8 GB of worktrees and tool output, .venv is 470 MB, .reference is 109 MB, .mypy_cache
# is 107 MB -- and a build sends the context to the daemon before it runs one instruction.
# A denylist would have to name each of those, and would silently ship the next large
# directory somebody adds. This names the three paths the image needs and excludes
# everything else by default.
#
# src/** rather than src: the pattern must match the files inside the directory, not only
# the directory entry.
#
# The last two are the model-catalogue bake step, and they are named as single files
# rather than as `!tools/**` and `!deploy/**` on purpose: this is an allowlist, and a
# directory glob would silently ship whatever anybody adds beside them next.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!src/**
!tools/bake_model_catalog.py
!deploy/k8s/model-gateway.yaml
